  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Changed this week",
      "items": [
        "Speed Check is new: drops a jump the Doppler speed cannot explain, which drew the 40-50 m spurs at junctions",
        "Drift confirm now scales with accuracy instead of a flat 15 m that sat below the gate's own error bar",
        "Backlog Flush sorts by recorded_at and holds live fixes for up to 60 s while it drains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Why send order matters",
      "items": [
        "Redis holds one position per truck and drops anything older than what it already has",
        "A live fix sent ahead of the backlog makes every replayed point stale on arrival, so the map draws a straight line",
        "Timescale stores the points either way: only the live view depends on order"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Two implementations, one behaviour",
      "items": [
        "JS runs the chain in the foreground, the native Android service runs it in the background",
        "js_alive plus a 30 s heartbeat decides which one records, so they never both publish",
        "Every constant is duplicated in backgroundGpsTracker.ts and LocationTrackingService.kt"
      ]
    }
  ]
